  (text "pole RX4 with CX3: 3.29 kHz\nzero (RX4 + RVX2) with CX3: 3.29 kHz (Tone 0)\nto 723 Hz (Tone 100)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 121.92 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "65900391-3c1c-5e00-a131-133e9a3fd707"))
  (text "CX4 with RX5: 4.82 Hz" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 119.38 104.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0b4853c0-83ad-53d9-bf3a-c2197ccbe1aa"))
  (text "Section 7 of the circuit notes. This is the shelf the DSP implements, H = (1 + s/wz)/(1 + s/wp), not the pedal's\ntone network: [2] describes a 20 kOhm pot between the op-amp inputs with 220 Ohm and 220 nF from its wiper to ground.\nRX4, CX3: the reported 220 Ohm and 220 nF [1], [5], used here for the fixed 3.29 kHz pole (inferred).\nRVX2: moves the zero from 3.29 kHz to 723 Hz; its law, 220 (4.55^Tone - 1) Ohm, gives the DSP's log sweep (chosen).\nCX4, RX5: the 5 Hz DC blocker after the shelf (chosen). Solving [2]'s network is the first open question." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 198.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "026e76f0-2f8f-5a50-a73b-926d6b4f9f95"))
